//--------------------------------------------------------------------
//---- Fixes 		 			 				 ---------------------
//--------------------------------------------------------------------

/* "Impound garages working correctly" (NTSC) **(debatable)**
 -- NOTEs;- --
 * This one from ntsc is same address but different value & instruction - thus it is impossible to convert without knowing what it should be.
 * There are too many variables to determine what is corect. Should ntsc be changed to reflects PALs default value or should pal be changed to reflect the NTSC fix?
 * SO i tried scrolling "up the stack" until it does that change / merge instructions thing.

// Impound garages working correctly (NTSC) **(debatable)**
//patch=1,EE,201C6088,extended,0C0BAA58 jal CGarages::IsPointWithinAnyGarage(CVector &)	|| NTSC 0C0BAA0C --> 0C0BAA58 or al,-56 (bytes OC AA) --> pop eax  || PAL 0C0BAA48 dec eax (bytes 48)
//patch=1,EE,201C63C0,extended,0C0BAA58 jal CGarages::IsPointWithinAnyGarage(CVector &)	|| NTSC 0C0BAA0C --> 0C0BAA58 or al,-56 (bytes OC AA) --> pop eax  || PAL 0C0BAA48 dec eax (bytes 48)
//patch=1,EE,201C6510,extended,0C0BAA58 jal CGarages::IsPointWithinAnyGarage(CVector &)	|| NTSC 0C0BAA0C --> 0C0BAA58 or al,-56 (bytes OC AA) --> pop eax  || PAL 0C0BAA48 dec eax (bytes 48)

--- "Up-The-Stack" Notes;- --
 * in PAL the instruction was already the same as the ntsc result after fix.
 * THUS i assume the PAL version is already by default correct IF ntsc is wrong by default.

NTSC;
instruction =	or r9,r10,[r8+r11*2]
* after fix becomes
instruction =	or r9,r10,[r8+ebx*2]

PAL;
instruction = 	or r9,r10,[r8+ebx*2]
* is already ^^ i.e. & does not change when switching 48 to 58 or the individual instruction from "dec eax" to "pop eax"
hex = 0BAA48C4

 -- Conclusion --
 ** PAL is Correct by default and does not require the fix up-the-stack, but might need the individual instruction changed from "dec eax" to "pop eax" or the bytes from -48 to -56.
 * NTSC by default is incorrect according to the author of the code BUT the Fix may also still be incorrect i.e. not same as pal
 -- what to do ? --
 * Leave PAL without the fix because it is not needed or change "dec eax" to "pop eax" or the bytes from -48 to -56 ?

// Impound check for NTSC by TKBS: 201C6087 0BAA48C4
//patch=1,EE,201C6087,extended,0BAA48C4	|| ntsc default = 0BAA0CC4 || PAL = 0BAA48C4 || TODO: Could also just use the BYTE addresss.
//TODO - check line 2 & 3

*/

