/*
	//--------------------------------------------------------------------
	// * WARNING: NTSC "Modern Widescreen fix.pnach" issues...
	//--------------------------------------------------------------------
	// 1. "fixes" - might not be required in PAL
	// * impossible to determine how and why some of these were implemented - assumption is they used decompiled source and some dev environment with ps2 dissamebler etc. but if based on PC source, that's not good.
	// * impossible to determine  if they are correct,... or actually required in other versions/ regions!
	// * as shown with the "impound garages" example below
	// - we do not know the differences between ntsc and pal source code builds, thus there is no way to determine which build offers the correct (or bugged) behaviour unless you know how to write assembly & convert it to MIPS.
	// - the authors refused to port the pnach to pal, or check them, or share any information on how they made them for others to replicate.
	// THUS the codes cannot be trusted to be ported to other regions/ verisons.
	// * the ntsc pnach patch authors have either failed to compare both versions, (or may have made fixes based on a region/ version comparison), and have left no information on how they make stuff
	// ** honestly i think the reason people do this gated shit is because they do not like it when people call them out for their mistakes or learn their secrets i.e. feed a false god complex.
	// ... thousands of people are zombies that do not know how to do stuff, by refusing to share they & the zombies enforce/ promote the idea that these patches are actually correct with no actual evidence of it.
	// The "menu - text body" has the same issue. the instruction is the the same at the same address, BUT other stuff in the stack is different, which leads to an incomplete OPCODE when straight porting due to the lack of information.
	//... it is also a fix that could and probably should really be a byte change only, no need for extended.
	// numerous 00000000's are refferrred to as NOP's, i see no evidence o fthis - Cheat Engine defines a NOP in GTASA as 90, not 00.
	// 90%+ of the codes i have ported to pal but something in the "//CRadar::DrawRadarSprite width" crashes.
	// ^^ Although i am pretty sure it does not do anything anyway.
	// I see no point in porting these;-
	"//CHud::DrawBustedWastedMessage width"
	"//CHud::DrawSuccessFailedMessage width"
	// when increasing FOV and screen size you want the messages bigger not smaller. You don't switch from 640x480 to 4k then use non-dpi aware and a font of 3 on a fucking 80 inch 8k screen etc, unless you have eyes like a fucking sparrow-hawk ...
*/

